{title: Oh My Darling, Clementine}
{artist: Traditional American ballad}
{key: C}
{license: Public domain: published in 1884}
{language: en}
{note: Chord arrangement by Petik}

{comment: Verse}
In a [C]cavern, in a canyon, excavating for a [G]mine
Lived a [G]miner forty-niner and his [G7]daughter Clemen[C]tine

{comment: Chorus}
Oh my [C]darling, oh my darling, oh my darling Clemen[G]tine
You are [G]lost and gone forever, dreadful [G7]sorry, Clemen[C]tine
